Z||000000||mope||10-09-2000||11:13 PM||||Is it possible to put a gt front bumper cover on like say a 84 or a 85se? or would it require more than just changing the cover? would it need diffrent front fenders too??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>thanks<P>m0pe<P>------------------<BR>--------------------------<BR>www.mastergraphics.cjb.net<BR>--------------------------||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||10-10-2000||01:14 AM||||Yes, it will work-no modification required. You will need the impact web behind it and the lower mounts to hold up the bottom along with the fender wells.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mope||10-10-2000||08:44 AM||||sounds good to me.<P>How much should i expect to pay for a front gt bumper?<P>i found one for 150 just needs to be repainted.<P>sound good???<P>thanks<BR>m0pe<BR><P>------------------<BR>--------------------------<BR>www.mastergraphics.cjb.net<BR>--------------------------||||reg||14
Z||000003||Tigger||10-10-2000||03:03 PM||||$150 doesn't sound bad for on that just needs paint.<P>You'll need GT front inner wheelwells or make filler panels from junk wheelwell plasic to fill the gap.<P>There are some lower brackets for the GT cover you'll need if they don't come with the cover.  Mainly it's the bracket that bolts the cover to the core support.<P>The crash bumper behind the cover from the SE needs to be cut down to make clearance unless you have the GT one.<P>Don't forget to find a GT cover with the ribbed or smooth side trim to match the rest of the car.<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tigger.gif">          <BR> <A HREF="mailto:RacingStripes@hotmail.com">RacingStripes@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
